Camoufox: the content-reachable file set must match a stock Firefox release.

Twelve chrome/resource packages are flagged contentaccessible=yes, so any page
can load their files as subresources and a file Camoufox adds or drops there is
a one-line build tell.

chrome://global/content/crashes.{html,js,css} were absent, because
--disable-crashreporter strips them in toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn. The
JAR_MANIFESTS entry is outside that moz.build guard, so shipping the three
content files does not build or enable the crash reporter.

The other tell this patch used to cover, browser-development-helpers.js, is
gone at the source: Camoufox builds with MOZILLA_OFFICIAL (assets/base.mozconfig),
which drops it exactly as stock does.

Guard: browser/tests/playwright/patches/contentaccessible-parity.py.

diff --git a/toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn b/toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn
index 641fcaa2fe..0d9f215fd2 100644
--- a/toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn
+++ b/toolkit/crashreporter/jar.mn
@@ -3,8 +3,6 @@
 # file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
 
 toolkit.jar:
-#ifdef MOZ_CRASHREPORTER
   content/global/crashes.html            (content/crashes.html)
   content/global/crashes.js               (content/crashes.js)
   content/global/crashes.css              (content/crashes.css)
-#endif
